Fix a soundness issue in the termination check of recursive calls in two-state lemmas and two-state functions: the caller's decreases clause was evaluated in its previous heap instead of the state the caller was entered in, so a two-state lemma could call itself with unchanged arguments forever and prove false, while some terminating recursions were rejected. The callee's decreases clause now also evaluates `old` in the heap of the call's label, if it has one.
